# Graphify corpus exclusions (ADR-051 p.7 — see vault:
# 04-decisions/adr-051-graphify-code-graph-adoption-in-code-repo.md). Same
# syntax as .gitignore. Merged with it and evaluated last, so this file can
# only ever exclude MORE; it can never re-include something .gitignore drops.
#
# Why a separate file and not a .gitignore line: graphify deliberately
# preserves git-TRACKED files against .gitignore rules, and .graphifyignore is
# the one input that stays authoritative over that exemption. The frozen
# generations below are tracked, so nothing else could drop them.

# Frozen module generations. app/m/v8 is the live mount; v1..v7 are history and
# are only ever read as history. Measured on the 2026-08-24 graph: 323 of 556
# scanned files and 2582 of 5324 nodes came from them, and an acceptance run
# sent 8 of its 38 lookups into v7 before it became clear v8 was the live one.
# Accepted loss, named in the decision: the graph stops showing that the freeze
# exists at all. That fact lives in app/index.html, which the tool does not
# parse anyway.
# WHEN A NEW GENERATION GOES LIVE, ADD THE ONE IT REPLACES HERE.
app/m/v1/
app/m/v2/
app/m/v3/
app/m/v4/
app/m/v5/
app/m/v6/
app/m/v7/

# The Android shell's staged web root — a byte copy of app/m/**. Measured: it
# contributes 0 files and 0 nodes today, because native/android/.gitignore
# already excludes it, so this line is inert on the standard run. It is written
# anyway for two reasons that are not: the graph's corpus should not depend
# silently on another subtree's ignore file, and --no-gitignore (which disables
# .gitignore and keeps this file in force) would otherwise pull the whole copy
# in behind a flag that reads as unrelated.
native/android/app/src/main/assets/public/
